  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T06:01:29.143Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe net taxable estate is ₱6,000,000 (₱12,000,000 gross estate minus ₱6,000,000 allowable deductions). The estate tax is computed based on the net taxable estate using the graduated rates under the Tax Code.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe computation of the net taxable estate and allowable deductions is governed by Section 34 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 34 of the NIRC, allowable deductions from the gross estate include various expenses and liabilities that can be subtracted to arrive at the net taxable estate. In this case, the gross estate of ₱12,000,000 minus the allowable deductions of ₱6,000,000 results in a net taxable estate of ₱6,000,000.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThe estate tax will be calculated on the net taxable estate of ₱6,000,000 according to the applicable estate tax rates. This means that the estate will be liable for tax based on this amount, which will be determined by the graduated rates specified in the NIRC. It is essential to ensure that all allowable deductions are accurately accounted for to minimize the estate tax liability.",
